## What changed from the previous draft

The revision makes five architectural corrections:

- It explicitly derives the lease protocol from the JIT authority pattern.
- It separates holder request facts from grantor-authoritative terms.
- It introduces a grantor-owned clock contract and service-point ordering.
- It turns eventual reclamation into an explicit, durable serving-composition obligation rather than treating every participant as advisory.
- It separates lapse from reclamation and adds fencing so delayed physical cleanup cannot preserve stale authority.

It also tightens status semantics. `:requested/:granted/:refused` describe negotiation; `:lapsed/:released` describe lease termination. `:rolled-back` is intentionally excluded.

